body:
Coordinator, merge note for head e97b5c5072fb04213bb6c7de879b4135a0fff1e1. Class: no refresh (the head is the reviewed head).

This merge relies on:
- the review marker on this head, and the read-only second read (no blocker);
- a trial merge here, on `main` fdda55e15 (the merge is clean):
  - the whole quick plan: 60 steps, 0 failed (37 post suites and 21 app suites, with `grblhal_post`, `tinyg_post`, `after_op`, `altmill_machines`, `first_router_part`, `conformance`, `post_spindle_rule_all`);
  - the whole post crate: 123 steps, 0 failed, with `grbl_family_same_tool`, `grbl_dialect`, `script_grbl`, `script_grblhal`, `script_tinyg`, `setup_change`, `first_traverse_clearance`, `tool_change_macros` and `recorded_streams`;
  - `golden_cl`, `posting`, `posting_rotaries_first`, the router binaries and the three example catalog suites: passed;
  - clippy on `camcraft-post` with all targets: clean. No golden file changed in the run.
- The heavy lanes are not a merge condition (#3556).

Not run: the light lane (its twins test `camcraft-motion`, which this PR does not change), and the app steps that the diff does not touch.

`main` moved after the trial by #3402 (2D Adaptive pass start). That change does not reach the post scripts. GitHub reports that this head merges with the new `main`.
